1
00:01:09,879 --> 00:01:11,079
Why look so grim?

2
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,480
Like you ate a basket of bitter melons.

3
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,680
It's not bitter.

4
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:22,959
It's suffocating.

5
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,760
If I hadn't heard about those three with my own ears,

6
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:33,879
I'd never have believed it.

7
00:01:38,359 --> 00:01:39,159
Yeah.

8
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,640
In all my years on the force,

9
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:44,239
it's the first time I've ever heard

10
00:01:44,599 --> 00:01:46,200
of a wimp being so "open-minded."

11
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,040
I just don't get it.

12
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,599
Did Zhang Baokui really do it?

13
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,760
Could there be a twist?

14
00:01:59,799 --> 00:02:02,200
If a pushover's nerves are stretched too tight

15
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,000
and snap,

16
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:05,480
it's not just a snapped thread.

17
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:06,599
The whole barrel blows.

18
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,319
Listen to you.

19
00:02:11,439 --> 00:02:12,240
As if

20
00:02:12,919 --> 00:02:14,560
you've lived through it yourself.

21
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,439
Zhang Baokui, we're the police.

22
00:02:27,719 --> 00:02:29,400
We have some questions about a case.

23
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:33,360
Han Yan already confessed her ties to He Yiqiang.

24
00:02:34,919 --> 00:02:35,759
Why we're looking for you...

25
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:38,639
you know full well.

26
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:39,680
I'm turning myself in.

27
00:02:39,919 --> 00:02:40,560
Hold on.

28
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,280
Get him on camera.

29
00:02:41,639 --> 00:02:42,520
You and He Yiqiang...

30
00:02:43,599 --> 00:02:44,639
what happened next?

31
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:27,639
Can you make a sound next time you come in?

32
00:03:29,199 --> 00:03:30,400
You didn't make a peep.

33
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,840
Are you a ghost or what?

34
00:03:40,639 --> 00:03:41,719
Just this?

35
00:03:42,319 --> 00:03:43,240
These two lousy dishes?

36
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,759
Just these two lousy dishes all day?

37
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:45,919
Do you even see me as an injured man?

38
00:03:45,919 --> 00:03:46,879
Do you think I'm healthy?

39
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,319
There isn't even any meat!

40
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,680
What kind of crap is this?

41
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:52,159
Who can stomach this junk?

42
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,240
Don't you have a fish pond?

43
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,199
Go fetch a couple of fish and cook them up.

44
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:57,520
Even frying up some fish paste would do.

45
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,599
At least it's something.

46
00:03:58,759 --> 00:03:59,879
Cooping me up in this dump,

47
00:03:59,879 --> 00:04:01,360
and there's not a soul around.

48
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,439
It's the middle of nowhere.

49
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,439
Do you want me to get well or not?

50
00:04:06,439 --> 00:04:07,360
What do you want?

51
00:04:08,159 --> 00:04:08,879
"What do I want?"

52
00:04:08,879 --> 00:04:09,639
What could I want?

53
00:04:09,639 --> 00:04:10,680
Look at what I've been reduced to!

54
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,800
What could I possibly do?

55
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,199
If you can't take care of someone,

56
00:04:14,199 --> 00:04:15,199
then get someone else.

57
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:17,959
Isn't Han Yan free anyway?

58
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,560
She takes better care of people than you.

59
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,879
I don't mean anything by it.

60
00:04:23,879 --> 00:04:25,000
Of course, with my leg right now...

61
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,319
You know what pathetic shape I'm in.

62
00:04:26,319 --> 00:04:28,079
Don't get the wrong idea.

63
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:29,920
What could I possibly do?

64
00:04:30,439 --> 00:04:32,519
She could come cook some decent meals for me,

65
00:04:32,519 --> 00:04:33,920
so I can get well sooner,

66
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:34,959
and I'll leave sooner.

67
00:04:34,959 --> 00:04:35,680
I won't be holding things up.

68
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,759
Then our business is settled,

69
00:04:36,759 --> 00:04:38,360
and I won't be in your way.

70
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:39,879
Won't be bothering the two of you anymore.

71
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,319
Isn't that great?

72
00:04:41,319 --> 00:04:42,199
Shut up!

73
00:04:47,839 --> 00:04:48,759
Losing your temper again.

74
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,240
Come on, what's your problem all day?

75
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,639
Can't you cheer up a bit?

76
00:04:52,639 --> 00:04:53,879
Why keep losing your temper?

77
00:04:55,439 --> 00:04:56,399
With you acting like this,

78
00:04:56,399 --> 00:04:57,079
let me tell you,

79
00:04:57,079 --> 00:04:58,959
my leg probably won't heal.

80
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,639
With this leg, for the rest of my life,

81
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:02,120
maybe...

82
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,040
I'll just stay right here,

83
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,279
and never leave.

84
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:07,639
Who wouldn't want to...

85
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,360
have a good day and be in high spirits?

86
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,680
I'm an injured man.

87
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:12,120
Shouldn't I get out for some fresh air?

88
00:05:12,439 --> 00:05:13,160
Have some fun?

89
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,560
There's not even anyone to talk to.

90
00:05:14,759 --> 00:05:15,360
Who doesn't want...

91
00:05:15,639 --> 00:05:16,240
Not even a wom—

92
00:05:19,639 --> 00:05:21,120
Don't push your luck.

93
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,399
I'm just messing with you.

94
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,279
Just joking around.

95
00:05:31,279 --> 00:05:32,040
Do you usually...

96
00:05:32,319 --> 00:05:33,040
never take a joke?

97
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:33,800
Look at you,

98
00:05:36,079 --> 00:05:37,160
always scowling like that.

99
00:05:37,399 --> 00:05:38,399
Just kidding!

100
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:42,680
Brother, how about this:

101
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,560
See how open and generous I am?

102
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:48,040
Don't worry about the cost, it's on me.

103
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,000
Drive me to a restaurant, will you?

104
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:51,240
The two of us can sit together,

105
00:05:51,639 --> 00:05:52,879
and have a few good drinks.

106
00:05:54,199 --> 00:05:55,439
We can get to know each other again.

107
00:05:55,519 --> 00:05:57,639
Because I feel you don't really know me,

108
00:05:58,199 --> 00:05:59,160
and I don't really know you either.

109
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,240
If things stay like this,

110
00:06:03,519 --> 00:06:04,720
my recovery will be slow.

111
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,079
Can we chat for a bit?

112
00:06:09,879 --> 00:06:10,560
Come on.

113
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,319
Brother?

114
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,120
Baokui.

115
00:06:27,079 --> 00:06:27,800
Baokui.

116
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,399
Baokui.

117
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:33,639
You always make me out to be

118
00:06:33,639 --> 00:06:36,199
a bad guy,

119
00:06:36,199 --> 00:06:37,360
petty and shady.

120
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,199
I'm not that kind of person.

121
00:06:38,199 --> 00:06:38,920
Let me tell you,

122
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:41,439
people from the Northeast have decency. Real decency.

123
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,240
Remember that.

124
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:47,800
Why do I keep asking Yan to come look after me?

125
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,040
Look at you, always making it

126
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:49,439
into something else...

127
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:50,759
You don't get it.

128
00:06:50,759 --> 00:06:52,439
Don't I want to get better soon?

129
00:06:52,439 --> 00:06:53,240
My leg, I mean.

130
00:06:53,439 --> 00:06:54,639
The sooner it heals, the sooner I leave.

131
00:06:54,639 --> 00:06:55,199
And here,

132
00:06:55,839 --> 00:06:56,319
every day,

133
00:06:56,319 --> 00:06:58,199
having you, a grown man,

134
00:06:58,199 --> 00:06:59,000
watching over me all day...

135
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,079
What's the point?

136
00:07:00,639 --> 00:07:01,279
It's completely unnecessary.

137
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,519
I'm not the kind of guy you think.

138
00:07:04,079 --> 00:07:06,199
Just go about your own business.

139
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,959
Yan doesn't need to—

140
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:10,879
she doesn't need to come every day.

141
00:07:10,879 --> 00:07:11,319
You know?

142
00:07:11,319 --> 00:07:12,000
Just every now and then,

143
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,519
drop by to take care of me.

144
00:07:14,519 --> 00:07:15,759
Besides, the two of us

145
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,759
already know each other.

146
00:07:18,759 --> 00:07:20,040
We can just chat.

147
00:07:20,319 --> 00:07:21,399
When I'm in a good mood,

148
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:23,279
my leg will heal faster.

149
00:07:23,279 --> 00:07:24,920
Neither of us gets in the other's way.

150
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,000
Neither of us wastes time.

151
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,439
It works out great for everyone,

152
00:07:27,439 --> 00:07:28,079
you know?

153
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,240
Just let Yan come over.

154
00:07:29,399 --> 00:07:30,360
Trust me on this.

155
00:07:30,399 --> 00:07:31,480
Nothing will happen.

156
00:07:31,839 --> 00:07:33,560
None of that nonsense you're imagining.

157
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,040
Come on,

158
00:07:34,399 --> 00:07:35,519
what are you thinking?

159
00:07:36,639 --> 00:07:37,120
That's just ridiculous.

160
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,360
I'm not that kind of person!

161
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,319
Sound good?

162
00:07:48,079 --> 00:07:49,600
Look how good you have it, right?

163
00:07:49,839 --> 00:07:50,319
Come on.

164
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:53,160
Cheer up, it's not what you think.

165
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,240
Would I ever be that kind of guy?

166
00:07:54,399 --> 00:07:55,360
I wouldn't do that to you.

167
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,680
I'm not that kind of guy.

168
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,160
Just tell her to come over, that's all.

169
00:08:02,279 --> 00:08:03,079
Baokui.

170
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,279
You're truly the best.

171
00:08:05,959 --> 00:08:07,000
So damn loyal.

172
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,160
Ever since you brought me back,

173
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,240
you've given me food and drink.

174
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:14,920
And now we're even Eskimo brothers.

175
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:15,600
Right?

176
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,639
Talk about keeping it in the family.

177
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,519
Whose wife would you say she is now?

178
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:27,079
If we say she's your wife,

179
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:28,680
you've got the certificate.

180
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,240
Right? You've got the legal status.

181
00:08:30,839 --> 00:08:32,679
But that's just a scrap of paper.

182
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,720
I had her.

183
00:08:35,559 --> 00:08:36,799
I touched her heart.

184
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:41,000
Just like your wife says,

185
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:43,360
Couldn't pry a peep out of him.

186
00:08:43,759 --> 00:08:44,279
Let me tell you,

187
00:08:44,279 --> 00:08:45,399
women need to be sweet-talked.

188
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:46,679
It's fine, I'll teach you.

189
00:08:46,679 --> 00:08:47,799
You've got to flirt with her.

190
00:08:47,799 --> 00:08:48,519
Chat her up.

191
00:08:48,519 --> 00:08:48,960
You know?

192
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,320
You can't just keep quiet all the time.

193
00:08:51,039 --> 00:08:52,360
Our wife falls for that stuff.

194
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,159
Quick, help me up.

195
00:08:56,159 --> 00:08:56,639
Help me down.

196
00:08:56,639 --> 00:08:57,720
I'm going inside to sleep.

197
00:08:58,679 --> 00:09:00,840
Great drinks today, had a blast.

198
00:09:02,519 --> 00:09:04,080
Our bond as brothers

199
00:09:04,799 --> 00:09:06,000
just got one step deeper.

200
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:09,120
Hold me up a bit.

201
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:10,159
My leg, watch my leg.

202
00:09:12,039 --> 00:09:13,679
Where else could I find a brother like you?

203
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:15,039
Seriously.

204
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,279
You're so genuine.

205
00:09:16,279 --> 00:09:17,120
So today,

206
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,440
I won't give you

207
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,879
any of that bullshit.

208
00:09:20,159 --> 00:09:22,240
Let's lay it all out on the table.

209
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,360
Since we've gotten to this point,

210
00:09:23,639 --> 00:09:24,759
go home tonight and have

211
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:26,360
Yan come over to keep me company.

212
00:09:26,639 --> 00:09:28,240
Then you can take her back tomorrow.

213
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,159
We can take shifts, take turns.

214
00:09:30,519 --> 00:09:31,679
Go on, don't worry about me.

215
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,240
We'll alternate nights, deal?

216
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,240
Hurry up and bring her over.

217
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:38,919
Baokui.

218
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:39,799
Baokui!

219
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,320
What are you doing?

220
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,799
My wife...

221
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:50,159
She's my wife!

222
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,440
You're back.

223
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:33,840
What are you doing?

224
00:10:35,519 --> 00:10:37,279
My car's stuck in the mud.

225
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:39,000
Hurry up and go.

226
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:39,919
Dinner's ready.

227
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,799
Make it quick.

228
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,639
The Zhang Baokui case.

229
00:11:34,679 --> 00:11:36,039
That makes 11.

230
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:18,320
Police! Don't move!

231
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:20,799
I never thought

232
00:13:23,519 --> 00:13:24,799
I'd be the twelfth.

233
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:12,960
The 2003 brick factory murder case.

234
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:15,960
Victims: Luo Xing and Xu Xiaoguan.

235
00:14:16,639 --> 00:14:19,600
You put them in the kiln and burned them into bricks.

236
00:14:21,559 --> 00:14:24,679
The informant was your wife, Ms. Pan.

237
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:27,639
Criminal suspect: Li Liang.

238
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:39,200
Was it you?

239
00:14:41,679 --> 00:14:43,879
Now you've murdered an

240
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,480
outstanding police officer.

241
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,639
Compounding your crimes,

242
00:14:51,639 --> 00:14:53,000
your days are numbered.

243
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:33,759
Push!

244
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:34,679
That's it!

245
00:15:35,279 --> 00:15:35,720
Push harder!

246
00:15:35,879 --> 00:15:36,320
That's right!

247
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:37,879
Keep going!

248
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:38,559
Come on!

249
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:39,639
Almost!

250
00:15:40,279 --> 00:15:41,200
That's it, push!

251
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:41,919
Come on!

252
00:15:42,559 --> 00:15:43,360
Yes!

253
00:15:44,159 --> 00:15:45,200
The baby's almost out!

254
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:45,840
Come on!

255
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:46,799
Push!

256
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:48,080
Come on!

257
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:58,279
Dongmei, congratulations!

258
00:15:58,279 --> 00:16:00,000
You finally had a boy!

259
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,840
Better days are ahead!

260
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,000
Get some good rest now.

261
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,639
I'll head downstairs first.

262
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,440
Excuse me, ma'am,

263
00:16:49,559 --> 00:16:50,480
how do I get to the village committee?

264
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:53,080
Well...

265
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:55,000
Turn right up ahead,

266
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,039
then take a left,

267
00:16:56,039 --> 00:16:56,799
and you're right there.

268
00:16:56,799 --> 00:16:57,519
Thanks.

269
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:10,119
You've got some nerve.

270
00:17:10,119 --> 00:17:11,680
Got some nerve now, huh?

271
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,400
Some guy just asks for directions,

272
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,319
and your face...

273
00:17:15,759 --> 00:17:17,640
you smiled so damn bright.

274
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:18,839
You...

275
00:17:18,839 --> 00:17:20,480
Why've you never smiled like that at me?

276
00:17:22,079 --> 00:17:22,680
Smile.

277
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:23,920
Smile for me.

278
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:29,559
Look at me.

279
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,799
Look at me!

280
00:17:38,119 --> 00:17:39,880
If you ever dare cheat on me,

281
00:17:42,039 --> 00:17:43,680
I'll bury you alive.

282
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,039
Burying me alive is nothing!

283
00:17:48,279 --> 00:17:48,920
What did you say?

284
00:17:50,039 --> 00:17:50,640
What did you just say?

285
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:51,319
Say that again!

286
00:17:51,839 --> 00:17:53,119
I'll kill you! I'll...

